comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T17:23:37.509Z","harness:claude-code","Partially delivered 2026-08-07 by child pm-z0cfor, which is closed with linked script, declaration and spec artifacts. AC1, AC2, AC3 and AC5 are satisfied: a declaration may carry a floor, the evaluator reports floor_undercut, the re-baseline path raises floors and never lowers them, the negative control proves both directions fail, and the violation line names its polarity.\n\nAC4 is half satisfied and the remaining half is genuinely blocked rather than deferred. graph-profile-edges-floor is declared at 11,318 and graph-profile-nodes-floor at 2,368, both baselined from the gate's own commit view, so a change that strips typed relationships now fails before merge. The second clause of AC4 — the count of active items resolving to an outcome, declared as a floor — cannot be written yet, because the only graph surface this gate can read is the audit profile and that object exposes no reachability field. pm-4vz6mz owns exposing it. This item stays open on that clause alone.\n\nWorth recording for whoever picks it up: the polarity fix makes the enforcement layer able to protect a magnitude in both directions, and a magnitude is still all it can protect. Typed reachability, dominance and articulation are properties of paths, trees and connectivity, and none of them is an integer compared against another integer. That is the general form, recorded as horizon AF on pm-doxj, and it is upstream of this item rather than inside it."
  "2026-08-12T22:09:15.237Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-08-13: the closed pm-z0cfor predecessor already delivered dual polarity; this branch owns only the remaining acceptance clause by exposing terminal outcome reachability in graph audit and ratcheting it with a native assurance floor."
  "2026-08-12T23:27:44.939Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence: the native assurance gate declares total directed edge count, active outcome reachability, terminal outcome reachability, and outcome node count as floors. All floor assertions pass at the live corpus values (12,103 edges; 335 active reachable; 2,103 terminal reachable; 6 outcomes), every assertion has a proven failing negative control, and the linked structural suite passes 3/3. The prior child pm-z0cfor already proved floor rebasing and polarity-specific failure text; this tranche delivers the sole remaining outcome-reachability clause."
  "2026-08-12T23:33:39.876Z","harness:codex","Recursive correction: immediately after closing two successfully delivered reachable items, graph-active-outcome-reachable fell from 335 to 333 and the static floor blocked. No relationship regressed; only lifecycle status changed. The prior close is therefore reopened. This tranche will preserve the active reachable/unreachable counts for diagnosis, gate the active typed-reachability rate, and add an all-status reachable population floor that cannot fall merely because work completed."
  "2026-08-12T23:57:35.745Z","harness:codex","Final corrected-head evidence: pnpm lint passed with zero clones, strict 100% docstring/static quality, native tracker-context-quality (37/37 assertions with negative controls), graph composition, record integrity, public-surface, token-budget, and package-boundary gates. Full coverage passed 488 files / 7,236 tests at exact 100% statements (52,448/52,448), branches (38,516/38,516), functions (10,787/10,787), and lines (50,676/50,676). Linked structural tests passed through sandboxed pm test. Packed artifact, npx smoke (13 packages), and package-first dogfood (88 commands) passed. The lifecycle-stable floor is 2,438 reachable of 2,453 non-outcome items at 9,938 basis points; both lowered negative controls fail."
  "2026-08-13T00:01:40.558Z","harness:codex","Implementation PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/992 — lifecycle-stable all-status typed outcome reachability floors and corrected recursive acceptance."
  "2026-08-13T01:01:49.095Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence: duplicate related-edge measurements/assertions were consolidated onto edges-related; active-only sparsity and outcome-unreachable assertions are warning diagnostics under closed ADR pm-dczodv, while stable all-status outcomes and structural/integrity assertions remain blocking. Native tracker-context-quality and graph-composition gates pass."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-12T23:27:45.401Z","harness:codex","A quality floor is only trustworthy when its measurement is typed: hierarchy and implements edges may establish outcome reachability, while associative related edges must remain a negative control or graph enrichment can counterfeit strategy."
  "2026-08-12T23:46:18.250Z","harness:codex","Absolute floors over active or terminal graph populations are lifecycle-variant: closing reachable work reduces the active count and raises the terminal count without losing structure. Enforce floors over the all-status non-outcome population and its integer basis-point rate; retain lifecycle partitions for diagnosis."
